I want to install FreeBSD 15.1 on my Tuxedo laptop. I've already confirmed everything works, excluding only suspend/resume and I'm OK with this. I want you to generate runbook for me for that installation.

This machine has 64GB of RAM and 2 x 4 TB disks. I want to install root on ZFS with the following options and need to know how to do this exactly:

1. ZFS pool should be mirror of those two disks (so the capacity will be 4 TB).
2. It should use geli encryption - so there will be geli and mirror and ZFS will not be aware of encryption - it will be below.
3. It should use compression zstd-10, I prefer heavy compression algorithm (so not less compression, not default, rather higher, research says that above 10 gives little gain and way more CPU usage so either zstd-10 or even zstd-9 if 10 already gives very little gain at very high CPU cost).
4. Enable dedup in "sha256,verify" mode, I know it is memory heavy - I have 64GB of RAM and storage is 4T (64 times RAM).
5. /tmp must be on tmpfs (ramdisk) and its size must be 512M.
6. Enable flags like 4K sectors (ashift=12) and atime=off, possibly other recommended for my setup (mirror of 2 4TB disks, 64GB RAM, many small files, many possible duplicates, I have a lot of data to store - mostly programming and emulators, so also compression needed).
7. There should be no multiple pools for /usr, /var, /home - etc. There should be only one pool / (possibly also /boot but only if it is required for freebsd on zfs to boot). Possibly also EFI partition, so mirrored: a) EFI, b) unencrypted /boot, c) encrypted ZFS and root pools from those two encrrypted zfses.
8. No swap at all.
9. All of this must be set before install starts, so applies to all data, if cannot be done during setup, then give me commands that I need to execute in shell prior to starting setup. I will install from USB memstick.
10. Use packages (pkg) not distribution sets - I've used them already and they're working fine for me.
